WEBVTT

00:00.499 --> 00:03.919
<i>♪ It seems today that all you see ♪</i>

00:03.921 --> 00:06.990
<i>♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪</i>

00:06.991 --> 00:10.494
<i>♪ But where are those good
old-fashioned values ♪</i>

00:10.495 --> 00:13.663
<i>♪ On which we used to rely? ♪</i>

00:13.664 --> 00:16.901
<i>♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪</i>

00:16.902 --> 00:20.670
<i>♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪</i>

00:20.671 --> 00:22.105
<i>♪ All the things that make us ♪</i>

00:22.106 --> 00:23.940
<i>♪ Laugh and cry ♪</i>

00:23.941 --> 00:28.874
<i>♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪</i>

00:34.434 --> 00:38.121
<i>We now return to Sesame
Street, now on HBO.</i>

00:43.669 --> 00:46.297
Oh, hi, you guys. How was school?

00:46.298 --> 00:48.573
Honestly, Mom, today was kind of weird.

00:48.574 --> 00:50.244
Every kid in school had to write a list

00:50.245 --> 00:52.409
of five reasons Principal
Shepherd is cool

00:52.410 --> 00:54.146
and then have their parents sign it.

00:54.147 --> 00:56.082
What? That seems crazy.

00:56.083 --> 00:57.949
One time, I saw him pee in a urinal

00:57.950 --> 00:59.317
with his hands on his hips.

00:59.318 --> 01:00.643
That's pretty boss.

01:00.644 --> 01:03.205
Why would the principal make
all the students do that?

01:03.206 --> 01:04.339
I don't know.

01:04.340 --> 01:06.007
I think he's going through a tough time.

01:06.008 --> 01:07.542
He's in the middle of a bad divorce.

01:07.543 --> 01:09.110
What? How do you know that?

01:09.111 --> 01:11.312
He's actually been pretty open about it.

01:11.313 --> 01:12.847
<i>Good morning, students.</i>

01:12.848 --> 01:14.382
<i>Today at 3:30,</i>

01:14.383 --> 01:17.119
<i>James Woods High will be
hosting a cross-country meet,</i>

01:17.120 --> 01:19.654
<i>which also happens to be where Lorraine</i>

01:19.655 --> 01:22.456
<i>has threatened to take my
children, across the country.</i>

01:22.457 --> 01:25.160
<i>And here's today's
"Tuesday Trivia" question:</i>

01:25.161 --> 01:26.795
<i>Does this sound like yelling?</i>

01:26.796 --> 01:27.896
<i>Because, apparently, this sounds</i>

01:27.897 --> 01:29.482
<i>to some people like yelling.</i>

01:35.254 --> 01:37.339
All right, finally some peace and quiet,

01:37.340 --> 01:40.342
so I can buckle down and
get some writing done.

01:43.245 --> 01:45.080
- Hey, Bonnie!
- What?

01:45.081 --> 01:48.083
Listen to this. Say, "It's
all been a pack of lies."

01:48.084 --> 01:49.851
What? Why?

01:49.852 --> 01:53.154
Just do it! Just say, "It's
all been a pack of lies."

01:53.155 --> 01:54.989
"It's all been a pack of lies."

01:57.692 --> 01:59.927
That sounded really good.

01:59.928 --> 02:02.263
Thanks, babe. Hey, you know
what that song's about?

02:02.264 --> 02:06.200
Phil Collins watching some
guy watch another guy drown.

02:06.201 --> 02:08.837
And then, the next night,
he invited the watching guy

02:08.838 --> 02:10.671
to be in the front row of his concert

02:10.672 --> 02:13.941
so he could sing it right to him
and they could arrest the guy!

02:13.942 --> 02:15.876
Really? Why wouldn't he have just

02:15.877 --> 02:17.746
helped the guy who was drowning?

02:17.747 --> 02:20.047
I don't know, I think he was
on a bridge or something.

02:20.048 --> 02:23.551
Like, he could see it, but he
couldn't get there in time.

02:23.552 --> 02:25.520
But he let a whole day pass?

02:25.521 --> 02:27.254
Why didn't he call the cops?

02:27.255 --> 02:29.090
'Cause he was busy writing the song!

02:29.091 --> 02:31.225
Wait, if he just watched,

02:31.226 --> 02:33.194
doesn't that also make
him a little guilty?

02:33.195 --> 02:35.196
Look, I'm not saying we
wouldn't bring Phil Collins

02:35.197 --> 02:36.730
in for questioning.

02:36.731 --> 02:39.634
I feel like maybe this story is bogus.

02:39.635 --> 02:42.136
Hang on, let me check Snopes.

02:42.137 --> 02:43.771
Yeah, none of that happened.

02:44.940 --> 02:46.040
Hey. What's up?

02:46.041 --> 02:48.409
Well, I'm trying to work on a sequel

02:48.410 --> 02:49.826
<i>to The Old Man and the Sea.</i>

02:49.827 --> 02:51.445
Are you, are you allowed to do that?

02:51.446 --> 02:54.448
But I can't get anything done.
It's so damn loud around here.

02:54.449 --> 02:56.584
Oh, yeah, that's what Hemingway
used to complain about.

02:56.585 --> 02:58.886
"This Spanish Civil
War is just too loud.

02:58.887 --> 03:00.621
How am I supposed to get anything done?"

03:00.622 --> 03:02.223
No, I mean, it might sound silly,

03:02.224 --> 03:04.492
but I used to daydream that by now

03:04.493 --> 03:06.894
I'd have my own place
by a lake somewhere,

03:06.895 --> 03:08.629
an oasis where I could go to write.

03:08.630 --> 03:10.898
Pay the bills by renting out the rooms.

03:10.899 --> 03:13.067
Oh, like a B and B? That could be fun.

03:13.068 --> 03:14.635
What? What are you talking about?

03:14.636 --> 03:16.937
I'm talking about you and
me opening a B and B.

03:16.938 --> 03:18.672
Are you serious? That'd be great!

03:18.673 --> 03:19.907
Sure. It'll be fun.

03:19.908 --> 03:21.242
All right, let's give it a try.

03:21.243 --> 03:23.811
Can't be any worse than when
I was on the Night's Watch.

03:23.812 --> 03:27.200
Hey, guys, you all want
to say the oath again?

03:32.120 --> 03:34.355
For the watch.

03:34.356 --> 03:36.090
For the watch.

03:36.091 --> 03:38.325
For the watch.

03:38.326 --> 03:39.861
Hi, Brian.

03:39.862 --> 03:41.328
I'm the boring storyline

03:41.329 --> 03:43.030
of the fat guy that's
watching that girl.

03:43.031 --> 03:44.798
<i>And I'm Ballers.</i>

03:44.799 --> 03:47.501
Ow!

03:47.502 --> 03:50.456
I totally get it. You're
right to do this.

03:55.460 --> 03:58.179
Well, well, if it isn't Meg Griffin.

03:58.180 --> 03:59.947
Leave me alone, you guys.

03:59.948 --> 04:02.616
Relax. We're taking the
day off from bullying.

04:02.617 --> 04:04.236
Oh, thank God.

04:07.905 --> 04:10.958
Very funny. Who put the Ark
of the Covenant in here?

04:13.028 --> 04:14.795
Meg is so stupid.

04:14.796 --> 04:17.364
She couldn't handle the
glory of God's love.

04:17.365 --> 04:20.467
Students, faculty and staff
of James Woods High,

04:20.468 --> 04:22.137
does anyone know how to push down

04:22.138 --> 04:23.572
the backseat of a Highlander?

04:23.573 --> 04:26.575
I know I can make a bed in
there, I just don't know how.

04:26.576 --> 04:29.043
Oh, my God, Principal
Shepherd, what's wrong?

04:29.044 --> 04:31.680
I just listened to two
hours of butt-dialed sex

04:31.681 --> 04:34.149
between my wife and the ADT alarm guy.

04:34.150 --> 04:36.150
Why didn't you just hang up?

04:36.151 --> 04:38.752
Because I miss the sound of her voice.

04:38.753 --> 04:42.323
Oh, my God!

04:42.324 --> 04:43.591
<i>P.A.): Principal Shepherd,</i>

04:43.592 --> 04:45.025
<i>your wife is on the line.</i>

04:45.026 --> 04:49.414
<i>She says, "Uh, uh, oh, God, harder."</i>

04:55.686 --> 04:58.772
Man, I still can't get over
how perfect this place is.

04:58.773 --> 05:01.508
I know, it's going to be
such a darling B and B.

05:01.509 --> 05:03.577
I got the boiler up and
running, Mr. Griffin.

05:03.578 --> 05:04.912
Well, we don't have a boiler,

05:04.913 --> 05:07.381
but I can't wait to see what
you've done in the cellar.

05:07.382 --> 05:10.584
Oh, also, please rub the "H"
and the "C" off all the knobs,

05:10.585 --> 05:12.454
so people won't know what
the hell's going on.

05:12.455 --> 05:14.923
I want the first four
minutes of every shower

05:14.924 --> 05:17.076
to be confusion and anger.

05:21.212 --> 05:23.230
Welcome, members of
our school community.

05:23.231 --> 05:25.299
Let's call to order
this emergency meeting

05:25.300 --> 05:28.569
of the school board regarding
Principal Shepherd's meltdown.

05:28.570 --> 05:31.105
I know a number of our
students have felt

05:31.106 --> 05:34.808
"traumatized" by the
events of this week,

05:34.809 --> 05:37.779
and we take those
concerns very seriously.

05:37.780 --> 05:40.414
Lois, I'm done with my gum.

05:40.415 --> 05:41.483
I don't want it.

05:41.484 --> 05:42.817
But I'm done with it.

05:42.818 --> 05:44.318
Peter, shh.

05:44.319 --> 05:45.804
I'll take it.

05:47.339 --> 05:50.091
So, due to his erratic
behavior, we have placed

05:50.092 --> 05:52.894
Principal Shepherd on
indefinite paid leave.

05:52.895 --> 05:55.796
Typically, Vice Principal
McGuire would step in.

05:55.797 --> 05:57.798
However, I was informed earlier today

05:57.799 --> 05:59.900
that she was found dead in her car.

06:02.237 --> 06:04.938
Therefore, the board is
seeking a parent volunteer

06:04.939 --> 06:06.774
to serve as interim principal

06:06.775 --> 06:09.009
until a permanent
replacement can be found.

06:09.010 --> 06:11.478
Hey, Lois, maybe I should do
it. I've always wanted a job

06:11.479 --> 06:13.315
where I can let my dandruff go wild.

06:13.316 --> 06:14.649
What? No way.

06:14.650 --> 06:16.784
I'm not having my dad be the principal.

06:16.785 --> 06:18.353
How embarrassing!

06:18.354 --> 06:20.255
Yeah, no offense,
Peter, but I don't know

06:20.256 --> 06:21.822
