power over the bullies.

11:51.645 --> 11:53.445
Now, you little punks get to class.

11:53.446 --> 11:55.347
And if you see Miss
Millikan, tell her I said,

11:55.348 --> 11:57.116
"Hey, what's up?"

11:57.117 --> 11:58.818
Huh.

11:58.819 --> 12:00.285
Maybe you're right.

12:00.286 --> 12:02.688
Wow, Dad, that was really something.

12:02.689 --> 12:04.089
Miss Millikan's just a friend.

12:04.090 --> 12:05.491
Oh, I don't mean that.

12:05.492 --> 12:06.925
I mean the way you handled those guys

12:06.926 --> 12:08.294
that were picking on me.

12:08.295 --> 12:10.862
Really? I felt like I kind
of lost my cool there.

12:10.863 --> 12:12.164
Not at all.

12:12.165 --> 12:13.966
That's what you've got to do more of.

12:13.967 --> 12:16.601
- You were like a real principal there.
- I was?

12:16.602 --> 12:19.137
Yeah. In fact, if you're
gonna lead this school,

12:19.138 --> 12:21.473
you've got to know that
kids need discipline.

12:21.474 --> 12:23.342
Especially kids like them.

12:23.343 --> 12:24.876
And their friends, Jeremy and Bridget.

12:24.877 --> 12:26.379
Oh, really?

12:26.380 --> 12:29.448
Where might I find this
Jeremy and Bridget?

12:29.449 --> 12:31.483
I don't know, study hall, second floor?

12:33.987 --> 12:36.823
All right, listen up,
maggots! Fun's over!

12:36.824 --> 12:38.857
There's gonna be some
changes around here,

12:38.858 --> 12:40.693
and what better way to
show you I'm serious

12:40.694 --> 12:43.213
than to smash a desk
with a baseball bat?

12:58.827 --> 13:00.496
Oh!

13:25.422 --> 13:27.173
Okay, we'll pick this up on Monday.

13:27.174 --> 13:29.107
Do any of you know my wife Lois?

13:29.108 --> 13:30.909
Tell her I'm on the bats
and to come get me.

13:30.910 --> 13:31.928
She'll know what it means.

13:37.668 --> 13:39.136
Let's go. Keep it moving.

13:39.137 --> 13:40.969
Get to class. Hey, you.

13:40.970 --> 13:43.238
You salute that flag
when you walk by, kid.

13:43.239 --> 13:44.940
Loads of people fought for that thing,

13:44.941 --> 13:46.475
including yours truly.

13:46.476 --> 13:48.310
Y-You were in the service?

13:48.311 --> 13:51.379
I may have misunderstood
what "yours truly" means.

13:51.380 --> 13:52.814
Hey, Dad, listen.

13:52.815 --> 13:54.448
The four of us got together last night,

13:54.449 --> 13:56.985
and we came up with a
list of 11 students

13:56.986 --> 13:59.287
and two teachers that you
need to do something about.

13:59.288 --> 14:00.889
Maybe you should start
with Mark Rutledge.

14:00.890 --> 14:02.290
Why? What'd he do?

14:02.291 --> 14:04.426
He wouldn't kiss Ruth at
the Sadie Hawkins dance,

14:04.427 --> 14:05.727
even though she bought him dinner before

14:05.728 --> 14:07.229
at Walt's Roast Beef.

14:07.230 --> 14:09.064
Well, I don't see how that's
got anything to do...

14:09.065 --> 14:10.264
And he called you fat.

14:10.265 --> 14:11.600
Oh, I'm gonna squish him!

14:11.601 --> 14:12.801
That's right.

14:12.802 --> 14:14.603
Don't take any crap from anyone.

14:14.604 --> 14:15.803
Oh, I won't.

14:15.804 --> 14:17.672
I'm gonna take down all these punks,

14:17.673 --> 14:20.475
just like I did in my
1980s crime series,

14:20.476 --> 14:23.078
<i>Gary Ratowski, Hockey Cop.</i>

14:23.079 --> 14:24.446
Gimme that purse!

14:24.447 --> 14:26.157
Hey, criminals.

14:27.032 --> 14:29.150
Puck you!

14:32.255 --> 14:34.641
Get the puck out of my neighborhood.

14:36.542 --> 14:38.527
Go puck yourself.

14:39.529 --> 14:41.281
Uh-oh, here come the real cops.

14:43.383 --> 14:45.819
<i>Hockey Cop, not a cop.</i>

14:49.888 --> 14:51.706
All right, ladies, I'm going to put this

14:51.707 --> 14:53.341
as gently as I can,

14:53.342 --> 14:55.110
but it appears that someone's rectum

14:55.111 --> 14:56.711
fell out on the stairs.

14:56.712 --> 14:59.380
Now, whose is it? Be honest.

14:59.381 --> 15:00.682
All right, that's fine.

15:00.683 --> 15:02.450
But let's just agree on a rule

15:02.451 --> 15:04.653
that if your rectum falls
out on the stairs,

15:04.654 --> 15:06.054
it's on you to pick it up.

15:06.055 --> 15:07.688
Look at that, Brian.

15:07.689 --> 15:10.457
Our day has just begun, and
there's a line out the door.

15:10.458 --> 15:12.126
I know, we're raking it in.

15:12.127 --> 15:13.495
This is a hell of a lot easier

15:13.496 --> 15:15.129
than when I delivered
pizza in New Orleans.

15:17.399 --> 15:18.633
What the hell?

15:18.634 --> 15:20.969
<i>♪ We're all just blocking the street ♪</i>

15:20.970 --> 15:22.671
<i>♪ We're all just
blocking the street... ♪</i>

15:22.672 --> 15:24.906
Come on, I got to deliver this pizza.

15:24.907 --> 15:26.874
<i>♪ Five trumpets do the job of one ♪</i>

15:26.875 --> 15:28.643
<i>♪ We're all just
blocking the street... ♪</i>

15:28.644 --> 15:30.145
I need to be there in 30 minutes.

15:30.146 --> 15:31.245
It's a company promise!

15:31.246 --> 15:33.380
<i>♪ Half the band isn't in the band ♪</i>

15:33.381 --> 15:35.049
<i>♪ We're all just
blocking the street... ♪</i>

15:35.050 --> 15:36.384
Oh, thank God.

15:36.385 --> 15:38.552
<i>♪ One of us dropped a contact lens ♪</i>

15:38.553 --> 15:40.555
<i>♪ We're going back to
block the street... ♪</i>

15:40.556 --> 15:41.855
Ah, screw it.

15:41.856 --> 15:43.557
<i>♪ We won't stop blocking the street ♪</i>

15:43.558 --> 15:46.546
<i>♪ Never stop blocking the street. ♪</i>

15:49.415 --> 15:52.334
Okay, so I think Lee
Blanding gets detention.

15:52.335 --> 15:54.568
And for Jason O'Neil,

15:54.569 --> 15:56.238
maybe you could pants
him during an assembly.

15:56.239 --> 15:57.872
Yes, good. I like that.

15:57.873 --> 16:00.674
Oh, hi, you two. What
are you working on?

16:00.675 --> 16:02.009
Oh, nothing.

16:02.010 --> 16:04.745
I, um... I'm just helping Dad

16:04.746 --> 16:06.514
with his schedule for tomorrow.

16:06.515 --> 16:09.117
You know, he's really doing a great job.

16:09.118 --> 16:11.620
He's actually made the
school a lot better.

16:11.621 --> 16:14.355
Huh. Well, I got to
admit I was skeptical,

16:14.356 --> 16:16.758
but it sounds like things are
going pretty well down there.

16:16.759 --> 16:18.193
You bet they are.

16:18.194 --> 16:20.074
They'll go even better after The Purge.

16:20.075 --> 16:21.034
The what?

16:21.035 --> 16:23.063
Hey, Meg, how about one of these?

16:24.467 --> 16:25.734
One of them things, yeah?

16:25.735 --> 16:27.402
Peter, what the hell are you doing?

16:27.403 --> 16:30.438
Uh, he's just saying he
wants to use his key

16:30.439 --> 16:33.575
to drive me to school
tomorrow in his car.

16:33.576 --> 16:36.378
Peter, what exactly are you
doing down at that school?

16:36.379 --> 16:37.712
I'll tell you what I'm doing.

16:37.713 --> 16:39.480
I'm doing a great job,

16:39.481 --> 16:41.249
like when I was a pro football kicker.

16:44.320 --> 16:47.422
Yay! Now I can fist
bump with black guys.

16:47.423 --> 16:48.423
Nailed it, Peter!

16:48.424 --> 16:49.491
There you go!

16:49.492 --> 16:50.925
Yeah! We going to the club tonight?

16:50.926 --> 16:52.913
- Not you!
- Okay!

16:57.375 --> 16:59.401
Hey, Brian, what's a "splat job"?

16:59.402 --> 17:00.802
I-I don't, I don't know, Stewie.

17:00.803 --> 17:02.856
I'm worried that you're seeing too much.

17:04.323 --> 17:05.674
Good morning, ladies.

17:05.675 --> 17:08.076
Were the paramedics able
to resuscitate Lamar Odom?

17:08.077 --> 17:09.677
They're still working on it.

17:17.837 --> 17:19.321
He's tall, get it?

17:19.322 --> 17:21.323
Okay, show's over.
Everybody back to work.

17:21.324 --> 17:23.491
Yeah, about that. We got to talk.

17:23.492 --> 17:25.260
Oh, uh, sure. What's up?

17:25.261 --> 17:29.130
We just realized we can keep all
the money, take your house,

17:29.131 --> 17:31.833
and kill you if you try
to do anything about it.

17:31.834 --> 17:34.135
All right, we're just gonna step outside

17:34.136 --> 17:35.355
and figure out a counter.

17:38.474 --> 17:40.141
And they locked us out.

17:40.142 --> 17:42.277
What about my loaf of
cinnamon raisin bread?!

17:42.278 --> 17:44.697
It's mine! It's not for the whole house!

17:53.805 --> 17:56.024
Let's just go. They won.

17:56.025 --> 17:58.078
Oh, we'll see about that.

17:59.311 --> 18:01.529
Hello, I'd like to report a brothel

18:01.530 --> 18:03.815
operating on Route 6,
near Round Hill Road.

18:03.816 --> 18:04.818
Thank you.

18:04.819 --> 18:07.229
You want to eat mangled raisin bread

18:07.230 --> 18:09.671
across the street and watch
the cops raid the place?

18:09.672 --> 18:12.340
Yeah, I'd like that.

18:24.270 --> 18:26.322
Oh, here comes the UPS guy.

18:26.323 --> 18:29.391
Oh, I bet he's delivering those
marmalade jars we ordered.

18:29.392 --> 18:31.559
Doesn't that feel like
a million years ago?

18:31.560 --> 18:33.161
Yeah, we don't need those anymore.

18:33.162 --> 18:35.014
Sorry, just send them back.

18:37.750 --> 18:39.235
You can just do that?

18:39.236 --> 18:41.318
Oh, yeah, you can just refuse delivery.

18:41.319 --> 18:42.554
You've never done that?

18:42.555 --> 18:44.997
I-I genuinely did not
know you could do that.

18:44.998 --> 18:46.550
Well, you can. Anything you order.

18:46.551 --> 18:48.885
If you don't sign for
it, it has to go back.

18:48.886 --> 18:50.021
Everyone does it.

18:50.022 --> 18:51.655
Most of what America is now

18:51.656 --> 18:54.291
is just boxes going back and forth.

18:59.964 --> 19:03.133
Students, this is a
chair without a seat.

19:03.134 --> 19:06.069
Jeff Banfield, I'd like you
to please come down here,

19:06.070 --> 19:07.637
take your pants off and sit.

19:07.638 --> 19:09.506
Me? What did I do?

19:09.507 --> 19:11.242
You know what you did, Jeff!

19:11.243 --> 19:12.976
I don't even know what's going on!

19:12.977 --> 19:14.477
Just go, Jeff, or he'll start

19:14.478 --> 19:16.246
hitting that trash can
with a spoon again.

19:16.247 --> 19:18.566
That means now, Mr. Banfield!

19:25.769 --> 19:27.570
What is going on here?

19:27.571 --> 19:29.274
Just a little of the three "R" s...

19:29.275 --> 19:32.146
Reading, writing and
wrecking this guy's sack.

19:32.524 --> 19:35.444
The school board received
a very serious complaint.

19:35.445 --> 19:38.923
Mr. Griffin, you are hereby
relieved of your duties.

19:38.924 --> 19:40.810
A promotion?

19:40.811 --> 19:42.464
No, you're fired.

19:42.465 --> 19:44.392
We've reinstated Principal Shepherd.

19:44.393 --> 19:46.059
<i>Wait, he's back?</i>

19:46.060 --> 19:48.563
But he had that crazy
meltdown about his divorce.

19:48.564 --> 19:51.165
Yes, but then I went on
a sex trip to Thailand,

19:51.166 --> 19:53.601
and I banged all the
goofy right out of me.

19:53.602 --> 19:55.336
Wait. Dad's fired?

19:55.337 --> 19:57.055
Who did this? Who turned him in?

19:57.571 --> 19:58.968
I did.

19:58.969 --> 20:00.240
Hi, Mrs. Griffin!

20:00.241 --> 20:02.093
Hi. Hi, Patty.

20:03.144 --> 20:04.345
Why, Mom?

20:04.346 --> 20:07.315
Because what you and your father
have been doing is wrong.

20:07.316 --> 20:09.201
We'll talk about this at home.

20:10.803 --> 20:13.621
Well, I guess your mom
was right all along.

20:13.622 --> 20:16.257
I had no business running a school.

20:16.258 --> 20:18.526
Can I be honest with you, Dad?

20:18.527 --> 20:20.495
I thought you were awesome.

20:20.496 --> 20:22.930
You stood up for all the
kids who get picked on.

20:22.931 --> 20:24.799
<i>You stood up for me.</i>

20:24.800 --> 20:28.468
Wow, so... so you think I did
a good job being principal?

20:28.469 --> 20:31.791
No, you did a good job being my dad.

20:37.062 --> 20:39.146
Come on, Meg, let's go home.

20:39.147 --> 20:41.315
And next time I want to
get back at your bullies,

20:41.316 --> 20:42.950
I'll do it the old-fashioned way...

20:42.951 --> 20:46.406
As a grown man beating up
teenagers in a parking lot.

20:49.341 --> 20:52.660
I'm planning on dying tonight.

20:52.661 --> 20:54.813
What are your plans?

20:55.683 --> 20:57.684
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru